# cbftp Integration Guide

## ⚠️ Important Notice

**This is NOT an official, actively maintained feature.** The cbftp/UDP integration was **not designed** for slftp to serve cbftp - it is a "dirty" workaround that happens to work. The slftp developers **do not actively test or support** this integration.

Use at your own risk. If you encounter issues, you may need to debug and fix them yourself or revert to native slftp mode.

## Overview

When `EnableUDP=1` is configured in `slftp.ini`, slftp switches to **cbftp mode**:
- slftp handles: IRC announces → Rule evaluation → UDP commands to cbftp
- cbftp handles: All actual FTP transfers, connections, and file racing

This offloads the FTP work to cbftp but comes with important limitations regarding NFO-based metadata extraction.

## Configuration

Add to your `slftp.ini`:

```ini
[UDPConfig]
EnableUDP=True          # Enable cbftp integration
IP=127.0.0.1           # cbftp host
Port=5696              # UDP port for race commands
ApiPort=55477          # cbftp HTTPS/JSON API port
Password=<password>    # cbftp API password
```

## What Works

### Core Features (Unaffected)
- ✅ IRC announce processing
- ✅ Rule evaluation (allow/block decisions)
- ✅ Route calculation and speed-based routing
- ✅ Site status tracking
- ✅ Section matching
- ✅ Affil detection
- ✅ Pretime filtering

### Rule Conditions (API-Based)
These continue to work because they use external APIs:
- ✅ `tvgenres` (TVMaze API)
- ✅ `imdbgenre`, `imdbrating`, etc. (IMDB API)
- ✅ `mp3year`, `mp3lang`, `mp3source` (parsed from announce)
- ✅ All general conditions (section, group, size, etc.)

## What Breaks or Is Limited

### NFO-Based Genre Detection (BROKEN)
When `EnableUDP=1`, NFO download tasks are skipped or exit early:

| Condition | Type | Status | Reason |
|-----------|------|--------|--------|
| `mp3genre` | MP3 | ❌ Broken | GenreDirlistTask not created |
| `nfogenre` | MDVDR/MVID | ❌ Broken | GenreNfoTask not created |
| `mvidgenre` | MVID | ❌ Broken | MVIDTask needs slots (see below) |
| `mvidlookupdone` | MVID | ❌ Broken | MVIDTask needs slots |

### Code Details

**Tasks never created with UDP:**
```pascal
// kb.releaseinfo.pas
if not pazo.IsUDPEnabled then
  AddTask(TPazoGenreDirlistTask.Create(...));  // Skipped

if not pazo.IsUDPEnabled then
  AddTask(TPazoGenreNfoTask.Create(...));      // Skipped

// pazo.pas  
if not IsUDPEnabled then
  AddTask(TPazoSiteSfvTask.Create(...));       // Skipped
```

**Tasks that exit early (do nothing):**
```pascal
// tasksitenfo.pas, taskgenrenfo.pas, taskgenredirlist.pas, taskimdb.pas
if mainpazo.IsUDPEnabled then
begin
  ready := True;
  Result := True;
  exit;  // Task completes without action
end;
```

### MVID/TV Lookup - Partially Affected

| Task | Created? | Works with UDP? | Needs Slots? |
|------|----------|-----------------|--------------|
| `TPazoTVInfoLookupTask` | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ❌ No |
| `TPazoMVIDTask` | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ **Yes** |

**Important:** `TPazoMVIDTask` requires FTP slots to download NFO files. If you set sites to permdown (recommended with UDP), MVID genre detection won't work because no slots are available.

### Other Disabled Features
- ❌ Race stats in IRC (output suppressed)
- ❌ SFV verification tasks (skipped)
- ❌ Native FTP racing (`Tuzelj()` exits immediately)
- ❌ IMDB NFO leeching (task exits early)

## Site Configuration

### Recommended Setup

With `EnableUDP=1`, set all sites to **permdown**:

```irc
!setpermdown * 1
```

**Why?**
- cbftp handles all FTP connections
- Saves slftp resources (no login/bnctest attempts)
- Rules still work (permdown check is bypassed when `IsUDPEnabled=True`)

### Trade-off: Slots vs Features

| Setup | Slots Used | NFO Genre | MVID Genre | TV Info |
|-------|-----------|-----------|------------|---------|
| Sites UP | All configured | ✅ Works | ✅ Works | ✅ Works |
| Sites PermDown | 0 | ❌ Broken | ❌ Broken* | ✅ Works |

\* MVIDTask needs slots to download NFOs; with permdown sites, no slots are available.

**Bottom line:** If you need `mvidgenre` rules, you must keep sites UP with slots allocated, even with `EnableUDP=1`.

## Technical Details

### Task Behavior Matrix

| Task | Created with UDP? | Functions with UDP? | Needs Slots? |
|------|------------------|---------------------|--------------|
| `TPazoRaceTask` | ❌ No | N/A (cbftp handles) | N/A |
| `TPazoGenreDirlistTask` | ❌ No | N/A | N/A |
| `TPazoGenreNfoTask` | ❌ No | N/A | N/A |
| `TPazoSiteNfoTask` | ⚠️ Partially* | ❌ Exits early | ✅ Yes |
| `TPazoTVInfoLookupTask` | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ❌ No |
| `TPazoMVIDTask` | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ **Yes** |
| `TPazoImdbTask` | ⚠️ Partially* | ❌ Exits early | ✅ Yes |
| `TPazoSiteSfvTask` | ❌ No | N/A | N/A |

\* Created in some code paths but exits immediately without doing work.

### Rule Evaluation

Rules are evaluated regardless of permdown status when UDP is enabled:
```pascal
// rulesunit.pas FireRules()
if (not p.IsUDPEnabled) and ps_s.PermDown then exit;  // Only blocks without UDP
```

With `EnableUDP=1`, permdown sites still participate in rule evaluation.

## Migration Checklist

When switching to cbftp (`EnableUDP=1`):

1. **Review your rules** - Identify any using:
   - `mp3genre` - Will NOT work
   - `nfogenre` - Will NOT work  
   - `mvidgenre` - Will NOT work (unless you keep sites UP)

2. **Alternative approaches**:
   - Use section-based rules instead of genre
   - Use group-based allowlists/blocklists
   - Use `tvgenres` or `imdbgenre` (API-based, work fine)
   - Keep slftp native mode if genre rules are critical

3. **Decide on site configuration**:
   - PermDown (recommended): Zero slots, but no MVID genres
   - UP with slots: Works for all features, but wastes slots

4. **Configure cbftp** - Mirror your slftp site/section setup

## Troubleshooting

### "My mp3genre rules don't work!"
**Expected behavior.** MP3 genre requires `TPazoGenreDirlistTask` which is not created when UDP is enabled. Use section or group rules instead.

### "My mvidgenre rules don't work even though I have sites UP!"
Check that sites have `UseForNFOdownload` enabled and available download slots.

### "Sites show as down but rules still match"
**Expected behavior.** With UDP enabled, permdown sites still participate in rule evaluation (only FTP operations are disabled).

### "No race stats in IRC"
**Expected behavior.** Race stats output is suppressed when UDP is enabled. Check cbftp directly for transfer status.

## Summary

| Feature | Native Mode (UDP=0) | cbftp Mode (UDP=1) |
|---------|---------------------|-------------------|
| FTP Transfers | slftp | cbftp |
| MP3 Genre Rules | ✅ Works | ❌ Broken |
| NFO Genre Rules | ✅ Works | ❌ Broken |
| MVID Genre (with slots) | ✅ Works | ✅ Works* |
| MVID Genre (permdown) | N/A | ❌ Broken |
| TV/IMDB API Rules | ✅ Works | ✅ Works |
| Slot Usage | All configured | 0 (or keep for MVID) |
| Race Stats | IRC output | Suppressed |

\* Only if you keep sites UP with slots allocated (defeats purpose of cbftp mode).

